course: dictionary
lesson: 8304
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and roach is one of them. The words around it help you choose the right meaning. This is context at work, just like finding the clues in any other sentence.
explain: In a river poem, «Where the roach swim» tells you that a roach is something that swims. Under the green weeds in a river, it must be a fish. Ask yourself: what kind of thing is this word naming? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it fits.
explain: In North America, «roaches» usually means cockroaches, the brown insects that run fast and live in dirty kitchens. If a sentence talks about food left out, germs or pests, the insect meaning is the right one.
fact: Roach has more than one meaning, so the context decides which one is right.
fact: A roach can be a small silver freshwater fish with reddish eyes and fins.
fact: In Britain and Ireland, anglers, people who fish with a rod, catch roach in rivers and canals.
fact: In North America, «roaches» usually means cockroaches: flat brown insects with six legs that run fast.
fact: Cockroaches can spread germs, so keeping food covered and kitchens clean is important.
exercise: In the poem, «Where the roach swim», what is a roach? | A cockroach in a kitchen | A kind of tree | * A small river fish | A type of bread
exercise: An American says, «There are roaches in the kitchen.» What does roaches mean? | Sweet cakes | * Cockroaches | Silver fish in a river | Brown birds
exercise: Which words in the poem show where the roach swims? | Cool and dim | * Slushy green undergrowth | Cool and full | Here we keep our larder
test: Anglers catch roach in which places? | Tall mountains | Hot deserts | * Rivers and canals | Dirty kitchens
test: How many legs does a cockroach have? | Four | Eight | * Six | Ten
exam: A roach can be a fish or an insect; what helps you choose which one a sentence means? | * The context, the words around it | Ignoring the other words | Guessing from the first letter only | Skipping the whole sentence
